  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Sinocalycanchinensin G may interact with Protein-L-isoaspartate O-methyltransferase through a series of intermediate targets. Specifically, Sinocalycanchinensin G is linked to Phosphotriesterase, which is a target of veliparib, and to 2-keto-3-deoxy-gluconate kinase, which is a target of methohexital. Both of these intermediates are ultimately targeted by Protein-L-isoaspartate O-methyltransferase. Additionally, Sinocalycanchinensin G is also linked to Ephrin type-A receptor 6, which is targeted by a complex molecule that in turn targets the same enzyme. This indicates that the relationship between Sinocalycanchinensin G and Protein-L-isoaspartate O-methyltransferase is mediated through multiple pathways, with the enzyme being a downstream target of several distinct entities. The evidence is consistent across different scores, suggesting a plausible biological relationship, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be elucidated."
